# Q7 - production upload limits are shipped as managed server config and take effect

Revision: eca16dfd0e1eca3fed2200f5cb6026be711a45bf

## Managed PHP-FPM config deploy/server/php/caneguard-upload-limits.ini is the effective limit set
$ php -c deploy/server/php/caneguard-upload-limits.ini -r 'echo ini_get(...)'
  upload_max_filesize=20M post_max_size=24M
$ php -r 'echo ini_get(...)'   # stock host defaults, for contrast
  upload_max_filesize=2M post_max_size=8M

## nginx config deploy/server/nginx/caneguard-upload-limits.conf
  # Managed by docs/production-deployment.md (Server upload limits). Applies to every server block on this host.
  client_max_body_size 24m;

## Integrity manifest the administrator installs from (deploy/server/SHA256SUMS)
$ cd deploy/server && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
  nginx/caneguard-upload-limits.conf: OK
  php/caneguard-upload-limits.ini: OK

## End-to-end: a 9 MiB original photo (near the 10 MiB contract maximum) through the real API
   Photo on disk: 9437184 bytes, real JPEG 2000x2000

a) Server started with stock PHP limits (php -S 127.0.0.1:8124, upload_max_filesize=2M post_max_size=8M):
   POST /api/v2/mobile/reports -> HTTP 413
{"message":"The request could not be processed.","code":"HTTP_ERROR"}

b) Server started with the managed limits (php -c deploy/server/php/caneguard-upload-limits.ini -S 127.0.0.1:8123):
   POST /api/v2/mobile/reports -> HTTP 201
   persisted identity=01a1f9bf-74a3-71cd-8803-3290fb5d9f69 image.size_bytes=9437184 image.mime_type=image/jpeg

c) Adversarial: a 12 MiB photo still exceeds the contract's 10 MiB maximum (server limit is not a bypass)
   Photo on disk: 12582912 bytes
   POST /api/v2/mobile/reports -> HTTP 422
{"message":"The given data was invalid.","code":"VALIDATION_ERROR","errors":{"image":["The image field must not be greater than 10240 kilobytes."]}}
